# .cursorrules — Development guidance for Cursor AI

## Project context
Healthcare supply chain inventory AI agent for ~4,000 SKUs (SSM Health scale).
Python/LangGraph/Groq. All agent interactions go through agent/core.py.

## Architecture rules
- All LLM calls use Groq (llama-3.3-70b-versatile) via langchain-groq.
- Tools are LangChain @tool decorated functions in tools/*.py.
- Agent state is managed by LangGraph (agent/core.py).
- Database access uses SQLAlchemy sessions via `with get_db() as db:`.
- Never call the DB directly from agent/core.py — always through tools.

## Code style
- Use type hints everywhere.
- Tools must return strings (the LLM reads tool output as text).
- Use `Optional[str]` not `str | None` for compatibility.
- Keep tool docstrings precise — LLM uses them for tool selection.
- Tool functions should be < 80 lines; extract helpers if longer.

## Healthcare compliance rules to follow
- Always log DEA/controlled substance operations.
- PAR levels are the minimum safe quantity — never suggest ignoring them.
- Purchase orders created by the agent are always DRAFT — require human approval.
- Expiry dates must follow FIFO — document this in any expiry-related logic.

## Adding new tools
1. Create the @tool function in the appropriate tools/*.py file.
2. Add it to the ALL_TOOLS list in agent/core.py.
3. Write a test in tests/test_agent.py.
4. Update the SYSTEM_PROMPT in agent/prompts.py if the capability is significant.

## Testing
- Run: pytest tests/ -v
- Tests use SQLite in-memory via DATABASE_URL env override in conftest.
- Mock Groq API calls — never make real LLM calls in tests.

## Environment
- GROQ_API_KEY is required. Get from console.groq.com.
- Copy .env.example to .env and fill in values before running.
- SQLite is fine for dev. Use Postgres for production.

## Common queries to test manually
```
"What's below PAR in ICU-1?"
"Reorder all PPE below PAR"
"Which items expire within 14 days?"
"Run ABC analysis for surgical supplies"
"Transfer 100 units of SKU-00001 from Central Supply to OR-3"
"Are there any controlled substance tracking issues?"
```
